    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but isn't that distinction a bit of a fantasy? even if we want to \"expand who gets to create,\" the very definition of \"excellence\" or \"mastery\" is usually shaped by the institutions that hold the power—the major museums, the big collectors, the prestigious academies. if those institutions are fundamentally built on those exclusionary frameworks you're trying to separate from the skill itself, isn't any attempt to \"raise the bar\" just a way of reinforcing the same old hierarchy under a different name? it seems like it's impossible to have a \"universal\" standard that isn't inherently biased toward the people who defined it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
